, the record for Adams County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. August to September and November to December each came in under 90% of normal in 39 years. In 2025, January to February ran 22% of normal and August to September ran 30%. Grid 24154 had its driest year in 1988 at 53% of normal.</p>"}
